cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its recorded results, please cite it as below."
title: "olmoearth_inferenceX: label-free audit of Earth-observation prediction maps"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Qi
    given-names: Ziming
version: 1.17.1
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/2imi9/olmoearth_inferenceX"
url: "https://olmoearth-inferencex.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  A Python package for assessing classification maps from Earth-observation models. Without reference
  labels, it ranks a map's windows by the model's confidence for manual review, lists the cues behind each
  flagged window, and compares two maps of the same area. With a labelled sample, it estimates the error rate
  and per-class accuracy with confidence intervals, and identifies the largest high-confidence part of the map
  whose error rate does not exceed a specified level at a stated confidence; from labels drawn where two maps
  differ, it gives an interval on their accuracy difference. The methods are evaluated on the
  24 tasks of Ai2's published embedding suite across 16 encoders, on published land-cover and field
  maps against reference samples, and on deployed models, including a preregistered blind transfer
  test; the experiments, their committed artifacts, the claim ledger and the technical report are in
  the research record,
  https://github.com/2imi9/olmoearth_inferenceX-record.
